			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3829429">
									

<p>I love the atmosphere of this one, but I have a couple of issues&#8230; unlike Site 13 or the pipe death maze that also occasionally produces field mice, there's really no ticking clock to cause people to have to &quot;get out&quot; of this location, which means it could be explored a lot more.</p>
<p>Like, I'm confused about the (lack of a) seventh floor&#8230; if it's an old-style elevator, the sort that uses telescoping grates for doors, then there's no reason someone couldn't wait on Level 6 until the elevator goes up and abseil down the shaft to the seventh floor. And that's just the sort of nosiness that I'd expect from any halfway decent MTF or research team,</p>
<p>It seems really weird to have an SCP where they&#8230; didn't do that. &quot;Hey, we found this spooky but apparently safe foundation site we don't have any record of. There's a bunch of doors but they're welded shut, and we didn't try and open any of them, and there's at least one other floor but we didn't try to get to it. We're going to call it done, go get some Fish and Chips before we head home.&quot;</p>

